# Rust errors and tracing (kms-secp256k1-api)

## Errors

| Layer | Pattern |
| --- | --- |
| Library / services / traits / WASM / crypto | **`thiserror`** [`KmsError`](src/error.rs) + `crate::Result<T>` / `?` |
| Binary / `run_server` edge | Prefer `KmsError` or map `Box<dyn Error + Send + Sync>` once; do not add `anyhow` |
| HTTP routes | [`KmsError::status`](src/error.rs) + `Display` into JSON `{"error": ...}` |

- Do **not** return bare `String` from service traits.
- Do **not** introduce a second parallel error type.
- Prefer named [`KmsError`](src/error.rs) variants over `KmsError::Msg` when touching a call site.
- `# Errors` rustdoc must name failure modes (variants / conditions). Forbidden boilerplate: `Returns an error when the operation fails.`
- Proprietary WASM sources under `wasm-src/` are **never** versioned (gitignored); only host wrappers and committed `wasm/` binaries belong in git.

## Tracing

- Use `tracing::{info,warn,error,debug}!` for process logs. No `log::`. No `println!` for ops (test/debug harness output is fine when intentional).
- Levels: `error!` = operator-visible failure; `warn!` = degraded / skipped; `info!` = lifecycle; `debug!` = detail.
- Prefer `error = %err` (Display) unless Debug is required.
